---
title: "Data Lake Evolution: A Longitudinal Overview"
execute:
  echo: false
---





**Data Source Platforms:** The VISTA Oncology Data Lake integrates data from three primary platforms: **Genomic** data from Philips ISPM (IntelliSpace Precision Medicine), **Cancer Registry** data from NeuralFrame, and **DICOM Imaging** data from the Vendor Neutral Archive.

**Analysis Data Sources:** This analysis reflects PHI-scrubbed data from February 2025 to November 2026.

**Interactive Visualizations:** All plots in this analysis are interactive. Click on legend items to show/hide data series for better exploration.

## Data Coverage Summary

This longitudinal analysis tracks the growth and evolution of the VISTA Oncology Data Lake across eight data releases from February 2025 through November 2026. The dashboard monitors key metrics including:

### Data Completeness, Growth, and Platform Coverage
This report summarizes how the data lake expands and matures across releases, including changes in unique patient counts, case volume, and capture of key clinical events. It also highlights data completeness indicators such as follow-up, recurrence, and documentation depth over time.

Coverage is assessed across Cancer Registry (NeuralFrame), Genomic data (Philips ISPM and OMOP variant_occurrence), Imaging data (DICOM/OMOP image occurrence and WSI), and core OMOP clinical domains to show how multi-modal data availability evolves through each release.

### Key Metrics Tracked Over Time
The sections below focus on longitudinal trends in denominator growth, vital status and event recording, genomic testing and variant patterns, imaging accumulation, and release-over-release operational cadence. Together, these metrics provide a consolidated view of data acquisition, quality, and research readiness from February 2025 through November 2026.





